R5 2026.1-dev Build 10045 - USB channel layout
Audio settings can ask a USB sound device for stereo, 4 channels, 5.1, or 7.1. Automatic uses what the device reports. Restart media services to apply it.

R5 2026.1-dev Build 10044 - Latency save
The latency choice is saved for this account. Restart media services to use it.

R5 2026.1-dev Build 10043 - Finer MIDI
MIDI notes can use a finer velocity, and controllers a finer value. Programs that already send MIDI keep working. The Terminal command midi2test checks the new notes.

R5 2026.1-dev Build 10042 - Latency file
The latency choice is written into the sound settings. Restart media services to use it. A volume slider that starts from silence keeps a real level.

