Sound that does not match the mixer rate stays brighter. High quality follows the curve of the sound instead of a straight line between samples. The usual rate is 48 kHz. A late sound no longer leaves the mixer delayed.

A sound device plugged in after start shows up without restarting media services. A notification sound lets go of the mixer when it finishes.

